          <div class="kicker">Security & HIPAA Compliance</div>
          <h2>Not an afterthought. Foundational.</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">Role-based data isolation. Amendment-only editing on signed notes. A full clinical audit log. HIPAA isn't a checkbox — it's baked into the architecture.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <div class="feature-item"><strong>JWT authentication</strong> — 5-minute access tokens with automatic refresh. Sessions are secure, time-limited, and stateless.</div>
          <div class="feature-item"><strong>Role-based data isolation</strong> — enforced at every API endpoint, not just the UI. Providers see clinical data. Staff see administrative data. Patients see only their own records.</div>
          <div class="feature-item"><strong>Practice-scoped data</strong> — every query is filtered to the user's practice. Cross-practice data leakage is architecturally impossible.</div>
          <div class="feature-item"><strong>Amendment-only editing on signed notes</strong> — once signed, the original text is permanent. Changes go through a formal amendment process. This is the HIPAA standard — enforced in code, not policy.</div>
          <div class="feature-item"><strong>Clinical audit logging</strong> — every view, create, update, delete, print, and export logged with user identity, IP address, timestamp, and before/after values.</div>
          <div class="feature-item"><strong>Modern, maintained stack</strong> — Django 4 + Vue 3. Actively patched frameworks. No legacy code from 2006 hiding in production.</div>
        </div>
